<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Muslim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">executed 755</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Muslim was the Persian revolutionary leader who organised the Abbasid movement in Khurasan and led the uprising against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>. His armies were decisive in bringing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasids</a> to power in 750. His great influence made him a threat to the new dynasty, and he was executed in 755 on the orders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-Mansur.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abu-muslim.jpg" alt="Abu Muslim" width="317" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1598 author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Abu_Muslim_(d._755)_from_the_genealogy_(silsilan%C4%81ma),_Cream_of_Histories_(Z%C3%BCbdet-%C3%BCt_Tevarih,_1598).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The revolution was driven by widespread discontent with Umayyad Arab exclusivism, a policy that marginalised non-Arab Muslims, particularly Persian converts known as mawali, and was catalysed by the charismatic generalship of <b>Abu Muslim</b>, a commander of obscure but probably Persian origin operating from Khorasan.</blockquote><a href="/empire/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Abbasid Revolution, proclaimed in Khorasan in 747 under <b>Abu Muslim</b>, swept westward with extraordinary speed: in January 750 the last Umayyad caliph, Marwan II, was defeated at the Battle of the Great Zab, pursued into Egypt and killed.</blockquote><a href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Abu Muslim</b>, a Persian freedman of the Abbasid family, led the revolution of 747–750.</blockquote><a href="/societies/abbasid-caliphate">Social Hierarchy of the Abbasid Caliphate</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Abu Muslim</b>, who had risen openly against Umayyad rule under the Black Standard the previous June, took control of Merv and expelled the governor Nasr ibn Sayyar.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/february-14">14 February in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Abu Muslim</b>, a Persian revolutionary and military commander, began an open revolt against Umayyad rule.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-9">9 June in history</a></li></ul></section>
